---
// Naive append reallocations (11 copies) vs preallocated make([]T, 0, len(in)) (1 allocation).
const W = 900;
const H = 276;
---
<figure class="gtrsp">
  <div class="gtrsp-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Memory trace comparing var out []Item growing through repeated append reallocations versus preallocating make([]Item, 0, len(in)) once.">
      {/* Left panel: Unbounded append growth */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="430" height="248" rx="10" class="gtrsp-card is-red" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gtrsp-b-red">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Unbounded var out []Item (11+ allocs &amp; copies for 1,000 items)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Khai báo rỗng var out []Item (11+ lần cấp phát &amp; copy cho 1.000 mục)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="60" width="398" height="62" rx="6" class="gtrsp-box" />
      <text x="44" y="80" class="gtrsp-code">var out []Item // cap=0 initially</text>
      <text x="44" y="99" class="gtrsp-code">for _, x := range in {'{'} out = append(out, x) {'}'}</text>

      <rect x="30" y="136" width="398" height="110" rx="6" class="gtrsp-box" />
      <text x="44" y="158" class="gtrsp-b-red">Capacity growth waste cascade:</text>
      <text x="44" y="178" class="gtrsp-code">1 -&gt; 2 -&gt; 4 -&gt; 8 -&gt; 16 ... -&gt; 512 -&gt; 848 -&gt; 1280</text>
      <text x="44" y="198" class="gtrsp-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Discards 11 earlier arrays as GC garbage (~2x extra wasted).</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Vứt bỏ 11 mảng trung gian thành rác GC (~tổng RAM gấp đôi).</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="44" y="218" class="gtrsp-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Same pattern applies to make(map[K]V, n) &amp; Builder.Grow().</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Quy tắc y hệt cho make(map[K]V, n) và Builder.Grow().</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right panel: Exact capacity preallocation */}
      <rect x="460" y="14" width="426" height="248" rx="10" class="gtrsp-card" />
      <text x="476" y="42" class="gtrsp-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Preallocated make([]Item, 0, len(in)): 1 exact allocation</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Cấp phát trước make([]Item, 0, len(in)): Đúng 1 lần duy nhất</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="60" width="394" height="62" rx="6" class="gtrsp-box is-ok" />
      <text x="490" y="80" class="gtrsp-code">out := make([]Item, 0, len(in)) // 1 clean span</text>
      <text x="490" y="99" class="gtrsp-code">for _, x := range in {'{'} out = append(out, x) {'}'}</text>

      <rect x="476" y="136" width="394" height="110" rx="6" class="gtrsp-box is-ok" />
      <text x="490" y="158" class="gtrsp-b-ok">One straight write into slot [0 .. 999]:</text>
      <text x="490" y="178" class="gtrsp-m">1. Exact sizing cuts allocator churn by 50–90% cleanly.</text>
      <text x="490" y="198" class="gtrsp-m">2. No trailing 280 slack elements wasted past len(in).</text>
      <text x="490" y="218" class="gtrsp-b-ok">3. Even cleaner: let caller reuse slice `dst = dst[:0]`!</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Whenever input length is known upfront, preallocating slices, maps, or strings.Builder cuts heap garbage in half immediately without adding any complexity to readable Go code.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Hễ biết trước cỡ đầu vào, đặt trước dung lượng cho Slice, Map hoặc strings.Builder.Grow giúp giảm 50–90% rác Heap ngay lập tức mà code vẫn sạch đẹp như cũ.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gtrsp { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gtrsp-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gtrsp svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 680px; height: auto; }
  .gtrsp text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gtrsp-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gtrsp-card.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gtrsp-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gtrsp-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gtrsp-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gtrsp-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gtrsp-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gtrsp-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gtrsp-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gtrsp-code { font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: 11px; fill: var(--text); }
  .gtrsp-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .gtrsp figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
